  "decision": "accept",
  "icd10_code": "E11.22",
  "code_display": "Type 2 DM with diabetic CKD",
  "guideline_citations": [
    {
      "url": "https://www.cms.gov/files/document/fy-2027-icd-10-cm-coding-guidelines.pdf",
      "quote": "The classification presumes a causal relationship between the two conditions linked by these terms in the Alphabetic Index or Tabular List. These conditions should be coded as related even in the absence of provider documentation explicitly linking them, unless the documentation clearly states the conditions are unrelated or when another guideline exists that specifically requires a documented linkage between two conditions (e.g., sepsis guideline for “acute organ dysfunction that is not clearly associated with the sepsis”).",
      "source": "ICD-10-CM Official Guidelines for Coding and Reporting FY 2027"
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The chart documents uncontrolled type 2 diabetes mellitus (HbA1c 8.8%, on insulin lispro and metformin) and explicitly notes 'Developing diabetic nephropathy (eGFR 42, declining).' This constitutes a documented diabetic nephropathy/CKD diagnosis, satisfying the requirement for a CKD diagnosis (nephropathy) per the N18 rule. The eGFR of 42 indicates stage 3b chronic kidney disease. The follow-up sentence 'Diabetic peripheral neuropathy present' does not retract the nephropathy statement. The guideline presumes a causal relationship between diabetes and diabetic CKD, supporting the combination code E11.22. No negation, family history, screening, hypothetical, or resolved language is present. The evidence is sufficient for acceptance.",
